From 44903fb5088cc3ede1a7677763b4a452d066c87f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:06:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] RISC OS: platform support

Adds src/platform/riscos (built when CMake's RISCOS is set):
- stdout/stderr go to <Julius$Log> or /dev/null (nothing may print in
  the desktop; one write handle shared with dup2);
- the data folder comes from Julius$Data when no folder is given;
- a missing data folder is reported with Wimp_ReportError (SDL has no
  message boxes on RISC OS);
- spaces in file names become hard spaces ("North African.sg2"), as
  RISC OS filing systems store them;
- no file name case correction (RISC OS filing systems ignore case);
- the game draws its own pointer;
- each frame waits for the rest of its time (Julius$FPS, default 50)
  with SDL_Delay, which yields to the desktop: with no vsync the main
  loop otherwise runs flat out;
- with a log, a "Frames:" line every 10 seconds;
- the C heap goes in a "Julius Heap" dynamic area.
